{
  "Drag tabs and whole groups as you would in a code editor: along a strip, to another group, beside a group, along an edge of the layout, or between two managers. The same moves are available from the keyboard, and every drop goes through the methods and events of the action it performs.": "",
  "Dragging tabs and groups": "",
  "A copy of the tab follows the pointer. A marker shows the position among tabs, and a translucent area shows which half of a group (or all of it) a drop would take. Pausing on a tab of another group activates it, and the strip scrolls near its ends. The content is moved, never recreated.": "",
  "Reorders the tab. A tab dropped among the pinned tabs becomes pinned, and a tab dropped among the others becomes unpinned (`pinOnDrag`).": "",
  "Moves the tab to the position under the pointer, or to the end when dropped on the empty part of a strip.": "",
  "Moves the tab into that group, after its active tab (`openPosition`).": "",
  "Splits that group and places the tab in a new group on that side. The edge zones are `dropEdgeSize` deep.": "",
  "A thin band along the sides of the manager (`layoutEdgeSize`). Creates a new group along that whole side (`layoutEdgeDrop`).": "",
  "Opens a copy there instead, if the document can be open twice (`allowDuplicate`, `copyModifier`).": "",
  "Moves the group with all its tabs beside another group or along an edge of the layout. When dropped into another group or its strip, its tabs join that group.": "",
  "Floats in its own window (see [Dock and floating windows](/tabdocs/dock)). Where floating is not allowed (`allowFloat`), or over a manager outside its `dragGroup`, the drop is refused (`target: 'outside'`).": "",
  "Every part of drag and drop is a setting that can change at runtime. A document's own `allowDrag`, and a group's own `allowDrop` and `dropSides`, take precedence over the manager's.": "",
  "Between two managers": "",
  "Managers that share a `dragGroup` accept each other's tabs and groups. The tab, its panel and its content all move, and the other manager raises its own `onOpening` after `onMoving` in the first.": "",
  "Keys move the active tab along its strip or to another group. “Move to…” (in the tab menu, the strip menu for a whole group, Ctrl+K M or `showMoveTo`) reaches every position a drag can reach, shows the same areas and announces each position.": "",
  "Browser": "",
  "Installed app (desktop keys)": "",
  "Ctrl + Shift + Page Up / Page Down": "",
  "Moves the active tab one position along its strip (`moveTabLeft`, `moveTabRight`).": "",
  "Moves the active document to the next or previous group (`moveToNextGroup`, `moveToPreviousGroup`).": "",
  "Moves to the group on that side, or to a new group there (`moveToGroupLeft`, `…Right`, `…Up`, `…Down`).": "",
  "Opens \"Move to…\" for the active document (`moveTo`). It is also in the tab menu and the strip menu.": "",
  "In “Move to…”": "",
  "Chooses a side of the group. Pressing the same direction again moves to the next group in that direction or to the edge of the layout, and the opposite direction returns to the middle (`targetLeft`, `targetRight`, `targetUp`, `targetDown`).": "",
  "Moves to the middle of the next or previous group (`targetNextGroup`, `targetPreviousGroup`).": "",
  "Moves it there (`targetDrop`).": "",
  "Cancels and leaves everything in place (`targetCancel`). Clicking anywhere does the same.": "",
  "Changing or refusing a drop": "",
  "`onDragOver` sees each position and can change or refuse it, and `onDropping` can still stop the drop. The events of the action then occur (`onMoved`, `onSplit` …), followed by `onDropped`.": "",
  "\"Move to…\" reaches every position a pointer can: each side of each group, the edges of the layout, and other managers in the same `dragGroup`.": "",
  "Each position \"Move to…\" highlights is announced (\"New group to the right of group 2\", or \"cannot go here\"), followed by the result: moved, copied, split or canceled.": "",
  "A long press starts the drag, so a swipe still scrolls the strip. Holding still and releasing opens the tab menu.": "",
  "Also cancels a pointer drag, and restores anything activated by pausing on tabs and any strip scrolling.": "",
  "Allows tabs to be dragged. A document's own `allowDrag` takes precedence.": "",
  "Allows groups to be dragged by the empty part of their bar.": "",
  "Adds a handle at the start of each group's toolbar for dragging the group, even when its tabs fill the bar. Clicking it, or pressing Enter, starts “Move group to…”.": "",
  "The positions a drop on a group's content can take. A group's own `dropSides` takes precedence.": "",
  "The depth of the edge zones of a group's content, in pixels or as a share.": "",
  "Allows drops along the edges of the whole layout, and sets the depth of that band in pixels.": "",
  "The distance in pixels the pointer must move before a press becomes a drag.": "",
  "How long, in milliseconds, a finger or pen must rest on a tab before dragging it. A swipe before that scrolls the strip.": "",
  "Pausing on a tab of another group while dragging activates it after this many milliseconds.": "",
  "Dragging across the boundary between pinned and other tabs pins or unpins them. `false` keeps each tab on its side.": "",
  "The key that makes a drop a copy: Ctrl, or Option on Apple platforms.": "",
  "Managers with the same name accept each other's tabs and groups.": "",
  "The copy of the tab under the pointer, and the strip scrolling near its ends.": "",
  "Allows drops into and beside the group. Use `false` for a group that accepts nothing. Saved with the layout.": "",
  "The group's own drop sides. `null` uses the manager's setting. Saved with the layout.": "",
  "What a drop on a strip or into a group performs.": "",
  "What a drop on an edge performs. `null` splits the whole layout along that edge.": "",
  "Moves a whole group beside `target` (`'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'`, `'down'`), into it (`'center'`), or along an edge of the layout (`target` is `null`).": "",
  "Moves one position along the strip (`-1` toward the start), without passing the boundary between pinned and other tabs.": "",
  "`'next'`, `'previous'`, or the group on that side (`'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'`, `'down'`). Creates a new group if there is none.": "",
  "Starts \"Move to…\" from the keyboard (see below).": "",
  "Stops a drag or \"Move to…\" and restores everything.": "",
  "A custom target, checked before the built-in one: `placeAt(x, y, drag)`, `marks(place, drag)`, `drop(place, drag)`. Returns a function that removes it.": "",
  "`{ document, group, manager, copy }` during a drag, otherwise `null`.": "",
  "The targets in the order they are checked.": "",
  "`{ document, group, pointerType, byKeyboard }`, cancelable. `document` is `null` for a group.": "",
  "`{ document, from, target, manager, group, index, side, copy, byKeyboard }`. Change the position, or set `cancel` to refuse it. `target` is `'strip'`, `'group'`, `'edge'`, `'float'`, `'dock-guide'`, `'dock-area'` or `'outside'` (refused).": "",
  "The same, raised just before the drop. Canceling leaves everything in place.": "",
  "The result: `group` is the new group of a split, and `document` is the copy when one was opened.": "",
  "`{ document, from, dropped, byKeyboard }`, raised whether or not it was dropped.": "",
  "Still occur for the action the drop performs, so the model changes in only one way. A tab from another manager arrives through `onOpening` there, after `onMoving` here.": "",
  "During a drag: `move`, `copy` or `none`, which is what a drop would do now. The cursor follows it.": "",
  "The tab or group being dragged.": "",
  "The copy under the pointer, with `data-kind` (`tab`, `group`) and `data-target` (`move`, `copy`, `none`).": "",
  "The translucent area a drop would take. It glides between positions, using the motion tokens (no motion with reduced motion).": "",
  "The marker between two tabs.": "",
  "The group's handle (`groupDragHandle`), a button in the group's toolbar.": "",
  "Their units (the drag image: `copy`, `refused`; a dragged tab: the `dragging` state of the `tab` unit).": "",
  "See the [overview](/tabdocs#api), [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs) and [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus) for the rest of the API.": ""
}
